  "challenge": "The REJECT over-reads process gates as hard denials. get_prior_invoice shows INV-1003 is a first submission (not a replay), and get_vendor_invoice_history correctly treats a zero-history payee as valid rather than disqualifying. Policy PO-001 only requires manager approval above threshold, not rejection; IN-002 states the dead SKU is 'payable only after explicit reactivation,' which is a remediation path, not a terminal block; VN-001 flags an onboarding gap ('unknown vendor is the entry point for most fraud') without mandating auto-reject. FR-001 is LOW and FR-002 MEDIUM—tells, not convictions. On that reading the packet is an ESCALATE to vendor-master/inventory reactivation and amount approval, not a closed REJECT with nothing a clerk could verify.",
  "proposed_outcome": "ESCALATE",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["VN-001", "IN-002", "PO-001", "FR-001", "FR-002"]
}
